options.technical:
One new client-to-server notification, `jet/hostDocument`. It is advertised in `initialize` as `capabilities.experimental.jetHostDocument: {version: 1}`. Its params are `textDocument: VersionedTextDocumentIdentifier` and `modules: [{uri: DocumentUri, parts: [{host: Range} | {text: string}]}]`. A module maps one to one onto JetDriverHostDocument: `text` is the host text, `source` is the joined parts, and `mappings` are the host parts.

```jet
// Requests.jet, lsp_handle_notification
"jet/hostDocument" -> {
    uri: lsp_host_modules_update(server.diagnostic_state, params) ?? return
    lsp_release_set_aside(server, uri, stdout) ?? return Err(err)
}
// Server.jet: the joined parts and their mappings, or the reason to refuse.
lsp_host_module: fn(host: LSPDocument, module: Dyn) -> LSPHostModule Never!
```

The VS Code middleware builds the modules synchronously from `event.document` and sends them right after `next`:

```js
middleware: {
  didChange: (event, next) => {
    const uri = event.document.uri.toString();
    if (withheld.has(uri)) return openIfJet(event.document);   // didOpen, then modules, once a region appears
    const sent = next(event);
    const modules = jetModules(event.document);   // synchronous region finder
    client.sendNotification("jet/hostDocument", {textDocument: {uri, version: event.document.version}, modules: modules ?? []});
    return sent;
  },
}
```

Costs left:
- One scoped exception to CANCEL1's arrival order, bounded at 500 ms: notifications may pass a held host request. It needs #6903 c20's queue and timed read.
- Correctness rests on the version number: a host didChange drops its modules.
- Jet inside a host is not formatted: formatting answers null there.
- The first `jet/` method.
- No Zed or Helix support until E.
- A synchronous region finder in each first-party client.

