options.technical:
No new method. didOpen and didChange params gain an optional `jet` member, which servers that do not know it ignore; today's server does (review probe p3). The server needs no set-aside rule and no exception to CANCEL1's arrival order. Every host didChange must carry the member, because its absence means zero modules.

```js
middleware: {
  sendNotification: (type, next, params) => {
    const method = typeof type === "string" ? type : type.method;
    if (method === "textDocument/didChange") {
      const doc = workspace.textDocuments.find((d) => d.uri.toString() === params.textDocument.uri);
      if (doc && doc.version === params.textDocument.version) params.jet = {modules: jetModules(doc) ?? []};
    }
    return next(type, params);
  },
}
```

Costs left:
- A nonstandard member on two standard methods.
- Transport wrapping in Neovim and Emacs.
- Results vanish behind a tool that drops the member.
- No Zed or Helix support until E.

