briefings.body:
## Cycle p205 landed: dev 16c1bda2d9

**Landed (5):**
- the core-interface receipt's disposition table (Main);
- an erased trait value reports its concrete type (GoalsA-1-4, #6845 c14);
- the enum case catalog (GoalsA-1-4, #3147);
- one `jet inspect choices` JSON line per inlined call (PrecompiledCore-4, #6979);
- the tidy cleanup outside #6858 c2, with two lint false positives fixed (MemKernel-6-2).

**Suites on the p205 batch compiler:**
- golden: 4971 pass, 0 fail;
- core: all 2421 pass, the first clean core run this stretch;
- ui: 2841 pass, 17 fail (unchanged);
- cases: 4771 pass, 133 fail (one fewer).

1 new failure and 4 fixed:
- The new one is the Firefox notebook case. It and its Chromium twin swap between failing and skipping depending on which browser the host has. Both fail on the unbuilt `jet notebook` (#6418), so both are now marked known-failing.
- The fixed four include the TLS O0/O2 timing rows and the inspect-choices case.

**Speed:** a cold `jet run` of a small program takes 0.50 s at 313 MB. The InspectBuild check takes 8.42 s, down from 9.42 s.

**Criteria met:**
- #6501 c15: the B-step receipt, every row improved.
- #6845 c14: builtin types are Type values, and an erased trait value has the same TypeId.
- #3147 c4: case descriptors (EnumCases golden, O0/O1/O2).

**Found:**
- The disposition golden judges card references against a frozen board snapshot, rev 92504, that dev still tracks. Any audit citing a newer card reads as naming a missing card. The golden is updated in p206; the root is filed as #6311 c56.
- The nested tidy census (every package root) found 357 hits in 183 files. MemKernel-6-2 has filed fixes for all of them, so the #6858 c2 stack is complete and gets its own cycle, p207.

**The Any ballot (D-PRIM-ANY1):**
- Review 3 failed. Round 3 now recommends option C, a checked type arm over a trait value, with no Any type. A fourth fresh review is running.
- Filed from the probes: #6845 c15 (a method-less trait value prints empty), #6839 c32 (Core traits are refused as value types, against spec.md:938) and #6839 c33 (`Any` gets a bare E0119).

**Next:** p206 is running with nine SUBs:
- #6979 c1-c4 (inline census, refusals, Core `abs`), with a full suite and self-build;
- #6847 c4 and c9;
- #3147 c2 and c5;
- #6825 c1, c3 and c5 (G9 jobs);
- the golden and known-failing fixes.

## p202 landed (dev 7fbaac6e87, 11 commits)

**What landed:**
- **Precompiled Core:**
  - the taint-walk revert (it fixes the p201 sema.effects regression);
  - the lazy Core interface step (r2);
  - five fixed-cost cuts in the driver and loader: plan-lazy precheck, taint-walker state, launch environ, link-with-command move, and the web-target precheck;
  - cold rodata placed last;
  - the regenerated hot-text list (11,484 functions).
- **Test harness:** the minted-failure Trail snapshot fix, and host networking for golden rows that spawn a server.

**Suite against p201:** no new failures. Fixed: MintedFailureLeavesRun on o0/o1/o2.
- ui 2839 pass / 17 fail;
- golden 4965 / 3;
- core 2405 / 1;
- cases 4767 / 133.

The 3 golden FAILs are AppTypedArgs on o0/o1/o2. The row has never passed: p198/p199 ERROR, p200/p201 poll deadline, p202 the `wait` on a KILLed server compared against exit 0. Its fix (one case line) is in p203.

**Speed, p201 → p202 (A/B spans, RunColdContext `jet check`):**
- sema.effects 87.1 → 28.9 ms (p200 was 34);
- sema.finalize 288 → 231 ms;
- rcc wall 0.60 → 0.55 s at 314 MB;
- InspectBuild check 12.4 s at 3.04 GB.

**Precompiled Core receipts:**
- **#6759 c1: met.** comptime.bodies is 0.1 ms on both twins (1.26 s and 0.29 s on seed-b9). One comptime child per compilation, and all 20 Comptime examples match their goldens.
- **#6759 c20, strace half: PASS.** 0 Core or Prelude file calls in and out of the checkout. It closes on a clean O0/O1/O2 golden run (p203).

**Board:**
- #6978 (interned TypeIDs) moved to G11 by the speed-to-G11 order: days of hand work with a speed payoff. Its self-contained first part lands in p203.
- PrecompiledCore-4 moves to G6 #6979, the `#Inline(Always)` guarantee.
- **Any ballot:**
  - The first fresh review failed the draft, and its defects are filed as criteria on #6727, #6839, #6845 and #6833.
  - The redesign now recommends keeping the ratified rejection (no Any); a second fresh review is running.

# Status at 15:45: the speed sweep is building

**Self-compile speed:** there is no new number yet; the last measured rate is 8,510 lines/s. The new number goes here once two things finish:
- the full sweep's build (stage B);
- a cold comparison on a quiet machine: seed-b15 against the new compiler, on the same tree.

**What is landing:** sweep2, 106 changes, including:
- the first data-oriented compiler slices (#6793): S1, module IDs, and S2a, symbols carrying their module ID;
- generic Core readers and writers (#6759 c11);
- about 40 codegen and runtime improvements.

Stage A self-compiled at 15:25. Stage B, the full sweep built by the new compiler, started at 15:38. It lands on dev the moment it self-compiles, and seed-b16 is cut from it.

**Next, back to back:**
1. Batch 1:
   - the loop codegen regression fix and the guard fixes;
   - the dev server port, 345 → 158 errors;
   - the #3078 c13 and c14 settings work;
   - the Core-record fix;
   - the integer conversion change (#6313 c5b);
   - #6793 S2b.
2. Batch 2:
   - the From trait (#6313 c3) and the generic codec readers;
   - the record-brace syntax (#6251 c12 and c15);
   - the #3078 example programs.
3. seed-b17, then the last part of the From change.

**Goals (criteria met):**

| Goal | Met | State |
|---|---|---|
| G1 | 22/22 | Done |
| G8 | 110/110 | Done |
| G12 | 34/34 | Done |
| G4 | 59/61 | #5072 c64 is in sweep2; c65 is in progress |
| G6 | 358/697 | |
| G3 | 313/907 | |
| G5 | 252/813 | |
| G9 | 21/271 | |

Counts move once sweep2's proofs run after landing.

**Waiting on you:**
- D-WEBAPP-SHAPE1, posted, recommending A;
- D-BYTE-TRAITS2;
- D-HTTP-HANDLER-ENTRY1;
- D-PRIM-ANY1;
- D-GUARD-LINT1;
- the six D-SPEED ballots.

# Status at 21:05: overnight plan underway

**Stage 1: not done.** The full-compiler compile (L5) has never got past comptime body checking. Candidate **cand26f** is building now from live master, with three patches:
- **Keep-going mode:** one L5 run lists every error in every phase.
- **Comptime parity fix:** for the injected prelude error conversions.
- **Optimizer legality parity:** four Rust rules ported.

When it lands, the keep-going L5 run produces the first complete error list. Fixers are working the remaining known stop (the prelude `impl UTF8Error -> Err` body).

**Dev loop speed:**
- **Measured:** the frontend takes 240 s on a quiet machine; slower runs were contention.
- **Decode fix:** cuts decode from 105 s to 7.8 s on a replay of 2,697 real L5 reports, with byte-identical output.
- **SpeedHost:** building a speed-only host (smaller shards, stable unit text, the decode memo). It must be proven to produce byte-identical emitted Rust.

**Full Rust port:**
- About 50 Sol writers are running across the compiler, runtime, CLI, Tools, Jetpack and card lanes.
- The port wave started: 16 file-level packets are running now, out of about 40 queued so far.
- Everything is source first. Verification follows, as directed.

**Integration branch `integ`:** the held work and self-contained TANDEM Rust fixes land there, one checked batch per commit. See `~/.cache/jet-luna/INTEG-LEDGER.md`.

**Superlinearity:** being turned into hard gates:
- a growth exponent above 1.3 fails a cycle;
- a static checker with a required justification for every allowed exception;
- per-phase profiles.

**Owner actions:**
- **Ballots:** being finished with fresh beginner and adversarial reviews, then posted overnight. Priority order:
  - native substrate (#4494);
  - target facts and `usize` (#4483);
  - user-type map keys (#4499);
  - `IOError` `InvalidData` (#4409);
  - WIT export (#4493);
  - SQL safety (#4501);
  - Unsafe as an effect (#4502);
  - language in libraries (#4503).
- **New card #4500:** implement the ratified `@T` live links in both compilers.
